# Managed by Ansible (sssd role). Do not edit manually.
#
# Authentik's LDAP provider serves users/groups but not central sudo rules
# (see docs/plans/identity-authentication-architecture.md,
# 「Authentik単体で提供しない機能」), so sudo is granted here instead.
#
# The group is resolved through SSSD/NSS, so membership follows Authentik:
# adding someone to {{ sssd_sudo_group }} in Authentik grants sudo on every
# host running this role, and removing them revokes it (subject to the SSSD
# cache — see the role README).
#
# Password is required (not NOPASSWD): the password is the Authentik one, so
# sudo re-verifies the operator against the identity provider.
%{{ sssd_sudo_group }} ALL=(ALL) ALL
